d about them for a few hours  and  you know it's not something that you  would have seen under the previous  government  you're sitting in kabul and i want to  give you the last say as a young woman  in afghanistan right now knowing the  context of what's going on what is your  personal message to the taliban  my personal message would be that we are  not um demanding anything extraordinary  we just want our basic rights given to  us both to women and men  we just want that humanity or or  the basic rights given to us and for it  to be restored uh we're currently the  only country where girls are not going  to school and and i think that's crazy  in the 21st century  basic rights just give us the basic  rights to education health care and  just be nice to to your people in the  end of the day we're all afghans and we  we all just want to live in a peaceful  country where we all work together to  build it into a better better place to  be that's all i can ask for well thank  you for your message musca and thank you  for joining us muska gailani and graham  smith and thank you too for watching you  can see this program again anytime by  visiting our website that's  aljazeera.com and for further discussion  do go to our facebook page that's  facebook.com forward slash aj inside  story remember you can also join the  conversation on twitter we are at aj  inside story for me  tay and the whole team here in doha bye  for now  [Music]
 

